        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "bash",
          "code": "bin/kafka-server-start.sh config/server1.properties",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 7,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "kafka-cli-utilities",
      "heading": "Kafka CLI Utilities",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Create a Topic: Run the following command to create a new Kafka topic named DemoTopic with 1 partition and a replication factor of 1: This sets up a basic topic for sending and receiving messages. kafka-topics.sh --create --topic DemoTopic --partitions 1 --replication-factor 1 --zookeeper localhost:2181",
            "List All Topics: To view all topics currently available in the Kafka cluster, use: kafka-topics.sh --list --zookeeper localhost:2181 This helps verify whether your topic was successfully created.",
            "Describe a Topic: To inspect details of a specific topic, such as the number of partitions and their status, run: kafka-topics.sh --describe --zookeeper localhost:2181 --topic DemoTopic Useful for debugging and confirming topic configuration.",
            "Delete a Topic: To permanently delete a topic from the Kafka cluster. Be careful—this will remove all data associated with the topic. kafka-topics.sh --zookeeper localhost:2181 --delete --topic DemoTopic",
            "Write Messages to a Topic (Producer): To send messages to the topic, launch a producer using: kafka-console-producer.sh --broker-list localhost:9092 --topic DemoTopic You can type messages into the console. Each line you enter gets published to the topic.",
            "Read All Messages from the Beginning (Consumer): To consume and display all messages from the beginning of the topic: kafka-console-consumer.sh --zookeeper localhost:2181 --topic DemoTopic --from-beginning This is helpful for replaying historical messages.",
            "Read Only New Messages (Consumer): To read only the new messages that arrive after starting the consumer: kafka-console-consumer.sh --zookeeper localhost:2181 --topic DemoTopic"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 224,
      "subsections": []
    },
